    "bodyTextSample": "Compatibility\n\nFaceTec Device SDKs are compatible with most front-facing camera devices, and the FaceTec Server is supported on Windows, Mac, and Linux machines via Docker.\n\nAndroid SDK\n\nCompatible with ALL Devices with a Front-Facing Camera, Android 5+, armv7 or arm64.\n\nBrowser SDK\n\nCompatible with ALL Devices with a Front-Facing Camera on Supported Browsers, including laptops and mobile devices. See the matrix below for Browser compatibility.\n\niOS SDK\n\nCompatible with ALL Devices iOS 12+.\n\nFaceTec Server\n\nThe FaceTec Server is a Linux container supported by all major platforms via Docker.\n\nImportant Note: Windows Users may need to perform additional steps when running Linux Docker Containers on a Windows Host Machine. FaceTec recommends using a Linux Host Machine for an optimal deployment.\nCompatibility Matrix\n\nImportant Note: If you experience difficulties proving Liveness, this could be due to the Device running on an Insecure Environment, Malware, or Device Compatibility-related Behaviors. In these scenarios, FaceTec recommends trying to prove Liveness on a different Device as this will likely resolve the problem allowing you to successfully prove Liveness. Please reach out to the FaceTec Support if the behavior persists.\n\nYOUR DEVELOPER ACCOUNT\nAccount Info & Encryption Keys\nDemo Sessions Dashboard\nDEVELOPER GUIDES\nArchitecture: Features & Options\nCompatibility: Devices & Server\nTechnical & Hardware Details\nUX, Themes & Branding\nText & Language Editing\nOCR Templates & Creator\nSuccess Rates, Biases & Diversity\n2D Image Guidelines\nDEVICE SDK DETAILS\nGetting Started\nDown"
  },
